{
 "result": "fibmod.py is built and registered at baseline 14.99 (noise 3.5%). It reads whitespace-separated integers from stdin and prints fib(n) mod 1e9+7, one per line. It reduces n mod P=2(M+1), which is valid because M is 2 mod 5 so the Pisano period divides P. It precomputes three 2048-entry tables of (F(k*2048), F(k*2048+1)) style pairs over base-2048 digits of n, then combines three lookups per input. It passed the sample checks before assay. I am resting here because the table approach is already near its limit and a further gain would need more energy than the expected payoff justifies.",
